"'''Hello'''" is a song recorded by British singer-songwriter [[Adele]], released on 23 October 2015 by [[XL Recordings]] as the [[lead single]] from her third studio album, ''[[25 (Adele album)|25]]'' (2015). Written by Adele and the album's producer, [[Greg Kurstin]], "Hello" is a [[Piano ballade|piano ballad]] with [[Soul music|soul]] influences (including guitar) and lyrics that discuss themes of nostalgia and regret. Upon release, the song garnered critical acclaim, with reviewers comparing it favourably to Adele's previous works and praised its lyrics, production and Adele's vocal performance. It was recorded in  [[Metropolis Group|Metropolis Studios]], London.

"Hello" was a massive global success. The single charted in a record-setting 30 countries, including in the United Kingdom where it became Adele's second chart topper, following "[[Someone like You (Adele song)|Someone Like You]]"; it also had the largest opening week sales in three years. In the United States, "Hello" debuted atop the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], reigning for ten consecutive weeks while becoming Adele's fourth number-one single on the chart and breaking several records, including becoming the first song to sell over a million digital copies in a week. By the end of 2015, it had sold 12.3&nbsp;million units globally (combined sales and track-equivalent streams) and was the year's 7th best-selling single while it stands as one of the [[List of best-selling singles#Best-selling digital singles|best-selling digital singles of all-time]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.musikindustrie.de/fileadmin/bvmi/upload/06_Publikationen/GMR/Global-Music-Report-2016.pdf |title=State of the Industry Overview 2016 {{!}} Most popular artists and global bestsellers of 2015 |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2016 |website=[[Bundesverband Musikindustrie]] |publisher=[[International Federation of the Phonographic Industry|IFPI]] |page=7 |language=en |access-date=18 June 2022 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220205051734/https://www.musikindustrie.de/fileadmin/bvmi/upload/06_Publikationen/GMR/Global-Music-Report-2016.pdf |archive-date=5 February 2022}}</ref>

The accompanying music video was directed by [[Xavier Dolan]] and co-stars Adele and [[Tristan Wilds]]. It broke the [[Vevo]] and YouTube records for achieving over 27.7&nbsp;million views within a 24-hour span, and the record for the shortest time to reach one billion views (87 days) respectively.<ref name="Guiness">{{Cite web |title=Fastest time for a video to reach 1 billion views on YouTube |url=https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/413651-fastest-time-for-a-video-to-reach-1-billion-views-on-youtube |access-date=2023-02-09 |website=Guinness World Records |date=17 January 2016 |language=en-gb |archive-date=26 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230226174904/https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/413651-fastest-time-for-a-video-to-reach-1-billion-views-on-youtube |url-status=live }}</ref> "Hello" broke the [[iTunes]] records for being number 1 in most countries (102 countries).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Renshaw |first=David |date=2015-10-26 |title=Adele's 'Hello' breaks Vevo's most viewed record and goes to Number One on iTunes in 102 countries |url=https://www.nme.com/news/music/adele-157-1206055 |access-date=2023-02-09 |website=NME |language=en-GB |archive-date=9 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230209165215/https://www.nme.com/news/music/adele-157-1206055 |url-status=live }}</ref> The music video for the song received seven nominations at the [[2016 MTV Video Music Awards]], including [[MTV Video Music Award for Video of the Year|Video of the Year]] and [[MTV Video Music Award for Best Female Video|Best Female Video]].<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/articles/events/vma/7453279/beyonce-adele-lead-nominees-2016-mtv-video-music-awards |title=Beyonce, Adele Lead Nominees for 2016 MTV Video Music Awards |magazine=Billboard |access-date=26 July 2016}}</ref> At the [[59th Annual Grammy Awards]], "Hello" won three awards: [[Grammy Award for Record of the Year|Record of the Year]], [[Grammy Award for Song of the Year|Song of the Year]], and [[Grammy Award for Best Pop Solo Performance|Best Pop Solo Performance]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://pitchfork.com/news/71419-grammys-2017-adele-wins-record-of-the-year/ |title=Grammys 2017: Adele Wins Record of the Year |work=Pitchfork |first=Evan |last=Minsker |date=13 February 2017 |access-date=13 February 2017 |archive-date=13 February 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170213053522/http://pitchfork.com/news/71419-grammys-2017-adele-wins-record-of-the-year/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The song also won the [[Brit Award for British Single]],<ref name="McGeorge 2016">{{cite web|last=McGeorge |first=Alistair |title=Who won BRIT Awards 2016 Album of the Year? |website=mirror |date=24 February 2016 |url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/3am/celebrity-news/adele-wins-brit-awards-2016-7432961 |access-date=24 February 2016 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160225142925/http://www.mirror.co.uk/3am/celebrity-news/adele-wins-brit-awards-2016-7432961 |archive-date=25 February 2016 }}</ref> and [[APRA Awards (Australia)|APRA Award]] for International Work of the Year.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.smh.com.au/entertainment/music/apra-awards-2017-eccentric-musicians-sia-flume-troye-sivan-and-dd-dumbo-among-winners-20170403-gvcgfx.html |title=APRA Awards 2017: Eccentric musicians Sia, Flume, Troye Sivan and D.D. Dumbo among winners |work=The Sydney Morning Herald |first=Bernard |last=Zuel |date=3 April 2017 |access-date=3 April 2017 |archive-date=4 April 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170404074148/http://www.smh.com.au/entertainment/music/apra-awards-2017-eccentric-musicians-sia-flume-troye-sivan-and-dd-dumbo-among-winners-20170403-gvcgfx.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

